BCR adjustment to icu4c/source/tools/gennorm2/BUILD.bazel.

The `*.c` pattern in the gennorm2 srcs glob matches nothing: every source in
this directory is .cpp (see sources.txt). Bazel 8 defaults
--incompatible_disallow_empty_glob to true, which turns that into a package
loading error for anyone building @icu//... without the legacy opt-out. Drop
the dead pattern rather than set allow_empty so the glob keeps failing loudly
if the directory layout ever changes under it.

--- icu4c/source/tools/gennorm2/BUILD.bazel
+++ icu4c/source/tools/gennorm2/BUILD.bazel
@@ -14,7 +14,6 @@
 cc_binary(
     name = "gennorm2",
     srcs = glob([
-        "*.c",
         "*.cpp",
         "*.h",   # cannot have hdrs section in cc_binary
     ]),
